@meta
id: 07-01
title: The two ends of a long file
chapter: 07
type: lesson
skills: goto-line
par: 84
minutes: 6
vscode: Ctrl-Home and Ctrl-End
open: CHANGELOG.md

@brief
This changelog is 125 lines long. Everything you have learned so far moves
you by a character, a word or a line, and none of that is any use here: the
bottom of this file is ninety `j` presses away.

Two edits, and do them in this order.

  1. At the very bottom, the link reference for 2.6.0 is missing. Add it as
     a new last line of the file:

         [2.6.0]: https://git.acme.dev/orders/compare/v2.5.0...v2.6.0

  2. Back at the very top, line 1 lost its `# ` in a bad merge and the
     title is no longer a heading. It should read `# Changelog`.

Nothing else in the file changes.

@keys
| `G` | last line of the file |
| `gg` | first line of the file |
| `o` | open a line below |
| `I` | insert at the first non-blank of the line |

@hints
Two keys get you to either end of any file, whether it is twelve lines or
twelve thousand. One of them is a doubled letter.
--
`G` goes to the last line. `gg` goes back to the first. Neither takes a
count here — you want the ends, not a number.
--
Do the bottom first: `G`, then `o` opens a fresh line below the last one.
Then `gg` puts you back on line 1 and `I` starts typing in front of it.

@solution
    G o [2.6.0]: https://git.acme.dev/orders/compare/v2.5.0...v2.6.0 <Esc>
    gg I #  <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Around seventy keystrokes and sixty of them are the link line you had to
type. The travel — the part that would have been a scroll, a drag of
the scrollbar or a very long press on a cursor key — was three keys.

`G` and `gg` are the first motions in the dojo that do not care how big the
file is. That property is worth more than it sounds. Distance-based movement
(`j`, `5j`, holding a key) gets slower as files get longer, so you
unconsciously stop working on long files the way you work on short ones.
`gg` and `G` cost the same everywhere.

Two things to file away. `gg` is a doubled key because plain `g` is a prefix:
it begins a whole family of commands, and you have already met one of them,
`ge`. And `G` on its own means "the end", but `G` with a count in front of it
means something more precise. That is the next lesson.

@start CHANGELOG.md
Changelog

All notable changes to the orders service are recorded here. The format
follows Keep a Changelog, and this project uses semantic versioning.

## [Unreleased]

## [2.13.0] - 2026-08-14

### Added

- `OrderProvider.cancel` now records a cancellation reason.
- Customers can be looked up by external reference as well as by id.

### Fixed

- Refunds over 30 days old no longer fail silently.
- The order resolver no longer drops the `placedAt` field.

## [2.12.1] - 2026-07-30

### Fixed

- Payment webhooks arriving twice no longer create duplicate refunds.

## [2.12.0] - 2026-07-22

### Added

- Partial refunds, with an amount in minor units.
- A `refunded` status on the order entity.

### Changed

- `PaymentService.refund` takes an amount rather than refunding in full.
- Order search is paginated at 50 rows instead of 200.

### Removed

- The unused `legacyRefund` method on the refund provider.

## [2.11.2] - 2026-07-04

### Fixed

- Customer emails with a plus sign are accepted again.

## [2.11.1] - 2026-06-28

### Fixed

- The nightly reconciliation job no longer runs twice on Sundays.
- Cancelled orders are excluded from the revenue report.

## [2.11.0] - 2026-06-19

### Added

- An email receipt for every completed refund.
- `customerId` on the refund audit record.

### Changed

- Order ids are prefixed `ord_` on creation rather than in the resolver.

## [2.10.0] - 2026-05-30

### Added

- Bulk cancellation for orders stuck in `PENDING`.

### Fixed

- Timezone handling in the daily settlement export.

## [2.9.0] - 2026-05-12

### Added

- A GraphQL field for the payment provider reference.

### Changed

- Repository base methods take `{ where }` consistently.

## [2.8.1] - 2026-04-27

### Fixed

- A crash when an order had no customer attached.

## [2.8.0] - 2026-04-15

### Added

- Idempotency keys on the payment service.

## [2.7.0] - 2026-03-28

### Added

- The refund window, defaulting to 30 days.

### Removed

- Support for the v1 payments endpoint.

## [2.6.0] - 2026-03-09

### Added

- Customer notes, editable from the admin tool.

