# Changelog

All notable changes to the orders service are recorded here. The format
follows Keep a Changelog, and this project uses semantic versioning.

## [Unreleased]

## [2.13.0] - 2026-08-14

### Added

- `OrderProvider.cancel` now records a cancellation reason.
- Customers can be looked up by external reference as well as by id.

### Fixed

- Refunds over 30 days old no longer fail silently.
- The order resolver no longer drops the `placedAt` field.

## [2.12.1] - 2026-07-30

### Fixed

- Payment webhooks arriving twice no longer create duplicate refunds.

## [2.12.0] - 2026-07-22

### Added

- Partial refunds, with an amount in minor units.
- A `refunded` status on the order entity.

### Changed

- `PaymentService.refund` takes an amount rather than refunding in full.
- Order search is paginated at 50 rows instead of 200.

### Removed

- The unused `legacyRefund` method on the refund provider.

## [2.11.2] - 2026-07-04

### Fixed

- Customer emails with a plus sign are accepted again.

## [2.11.1] - 2026-06-28

### Fixed

- The nightly reconciliation job no longer runs twice on Sundays.
- Cancelled orders are excluded from the revenue report.

## [2.11.0] - 2026-06-19

### Added

- An email receipt for every completed refund.
- `customerId` on the refund audit record.

### Changed

- Order ids are prefixed `ord_` on creation rather than in the resolver.

## [2.10.0] - 2026-05-30

### Added

- Bulk cancellation for orders stuck in `PENDING`.

### Fixed

- Timezone handling in the daily settlement export.

## [2.9.0] - 2026-05-12

### Added

